{"content":[{"c":["BARSABAS*, BARSABBAS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Biblical surname. Barsabas (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") means “son of Saba” in Aramaic. Barsabbas, “son of the Sabbath,” is the preferred spelling in modern translations. Two people in the NT have this surname: Joseph Barsabbas and Judas Barsabbas (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.1.23","r":"Acts.1.23","rawR":"Acts.1.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.1.23","value":"Acts.1.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 1:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.15.22","r":"Acts.15.22","rawR":"Acts.15.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.15.22","value":"Acts.15.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:22"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Joseph_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Joseph_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Joseph_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Joseph #12"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Judas_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Judas_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Judas_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Judas #6"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BarsabasBarsabbas","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Acts 1:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.1.23","rawQueryValue":"Acts.1.23","sourceRefExact":"Acts.1.23"},{"anchorText":"15:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.15.22","rawQueryValue":"Acts.15.22","sourceRefExact":"Acts.15.22"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5b17a0bbe97de5a6a1bce74e93742f472251e00374f028ad5b8702c5cd707614","sourceItemName":"BarsabasBarsabbas","sourceItemOrder":90,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BarsabasBarsabbas","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"